When Claude Code was released last year, I felt i needed to learn. This will speed up my work as a programmer and widen my knowledge on some other tech tools I haven't exposed in the past. Now, AI is rapidly changing & evolving. I use AI as my speedy assistant but i am the decision maker. To illustrate: AI is my supercar and I am that cool driver. I don't need to know how to be a mechanic just to run this supercar. I rely relatively on its efficiency, comfort and looks. But still needs to gas up at a certain mile. That's AI. Humans created AI, that makes us far superior. So while AI makes my work easy, i do the judgment and i make AI follow my directions. And yes, i always have in mind when Claude says:  "Claude is AI and can make mistakes. Please double-check responses." 

I usually begin my design with Claude Chat. In plain language, i freely describe what i like following the rule: Assign a role, Provide clear context, Give examples if necessary and State dependecies/limits. Once that done, i usually make notes on the created docs until i get all the core functionalities and when i am sure it matches with the business requirement based on the data i gathered, i'd then transfer that to Chatgpt and let it attacked. After refinements made, both from me & AI, i will then ask Claude Code to create the application by providing the right stack to build on. 

AI acts as an agentic terminal tool that directly manages files, executes commands and handles complete dev workflows.
